Learning points
 ► Stiff- Person syndrome (SPS) is a rare neurological 
autoimmune disorder, which is often characterised by severe, 
unremitting pain.
 ► There is currently minimal evidence to suggest how patients 
with unremitting pain should be managed beyond first- line 
and second- line disease- modifying therapies for SPS.
 ► Serotonin- norepinephrine reuptake inhibitors may exacerbate 
symptoms associated with SPS.
 ► Magnesium sulfate infusions and ketamine may provide 
analgesia, spasm prophylaxis and early termination of 
exacerbations in SPS.

